# Every text file is stored with LF endings and checked out with LF endings.
#
# This is stated here rather than left to `core.autocrlf` because that setting is
# per-machine, and the repository has already been bitten by the difference:
# `core.autocrlf` is true in the Windows git config and unset in the WSL one, so
# staging the same working tree from the two machines produced CRLF in the index
# from one and LF from the other. `git diff --check` then reported every line of
# the affected files as trailing whitespace, which is how five files reached a
# commit that the hygiene gate would have rejected.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect binary content on its own; the explicit `binary`
# rules below still take precedence over it, because they come later.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets are declared as binary so that git, and the checks that use
# `git check-attr binary`, never treat them as text. Without this, a PNG is
# diffed as a wall of bytes and a text-only gate such as the trailing-newline
# check reports it as a missing final newline.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.pptx binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
